  @contract  ambient is the moves facility's alone: the share of its sonority a strand rests on  @ 2252
  @contract  returns the steps whose empty shortlists refused the solve, else nil  @ 2253
  @contract  widen stretches those windows to the nearest points instead, so none refuses  @ 2254
  @contract  selection must be exactly one grid column; multi-col selection is a no-op  @ 3052
  @invariant  a 1-col block stays contiguous when it lands on the destination col  @ 3053
  @contract  cursor follows to the destination column (single event and selection alike)  @ 3054
  @contract  refuse if dest col has any onset in source's row extent (note: note-on; else any event)  @ 3055
  @invariant  source's row extent = selection's [r1,r2] for a block, moved event's onset row for a single  @ 3056
  @invariant  tails (either direction) clipped by tm's tail pass; never block  @ 3057
  @contract  per-frame overlay for the chain the caret addresses: notes to ghost, cells to suppress  @ 3604
  @contract  the gate is fxHostAtCursor -- a cell that runs no chain of its own answers nil  @ 3605
  @contract  the window is the viewport's rows, resolved on the producer's own channel  @ 3606
  @contract  notes[colIndex][row] = tm's record by reference; note columns only; first onset wins  @ 3640
